{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואף כי אחרי מותי", :translit "v'af ki acharei moti", :gloss "and even more so after my death"} {:he "כ\"י שנים אחרי מותי", :translit "k\"i shanim acharei moti", :gloss "twenty[-one] years after my death"} {:he "יהושע פרנס את ישראל כ\"ח שנה", :translit "yehoshua pernes et yisra'el k\"ch shanah", :gloss "Joshua led Israel twenty-eight years"} {:he "וב' שנים האריכו הזקנים", :translit "uv' shanim he'arichu ha-zekenim", :gloss "and the elders extended two years"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אחרי מותי", :b "כ\"א שנים"}], :frame {:text "Joshua led Israel for twenty-eight years after Moses' death (Judges 2:8 implies he died at age 110; subtracting 40 years in the desert, since he entered at least age 20 at the Exodus, yields roughly 28 years of leadership). After Joshua's death, the elders who served with him continued leading Israel, as stated in Judges 2:7: 'And the people served the LORD all the days of Joshua and all the days of the elders who outlived Joshua.' Seder Olam Rabbah 11 calculates these elders extended Israel's period of leadership by some years beyond Joshua's own tenure.", :sources ["Judges 2:7" "Judges 2:8" "Seder Olam Rabbah 11"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "אחרי מותי", :a-value 675, :b "כ\"א שנים", :b-value 421, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:40:40.316425660Z", :model "glm-5.2"}